  "description": "60 generative artworks built on a very rare, hacked analogue video Wobbulator. The series is composed of both wild wave full-rides (1/1s) + bold bouncing screw-loops (editions)\n\nThe mint distribution pattern follows a 60hz waveform that flows out the 60 artworks through a modulating release sequencer - outputting both numerous 1/1s + editions of varying rarity.\n\n‘KARBORN developed The Wondrous Wobbulator Machine for Young and Old Alike in 2013 by feeding geometric still frames into a custom-made analogue Wobbulator - a hacked TV-like device that visualizes the wavelengths of any given sound frequency, to generate an electric series of bold-vibrating-video-graphic-artworks.’\n\nThe idea of ‘prepared televisions’ was first introduced by Nam June Paik and Shuya Abe in the 1970’s. By its nature as a handmade/hacked unit, each Wobbulator is unique - characterized by the tone and quality of its output. This is the first time a Wobbulator has surfaced on-chain. ZAP!!",
